! Field Collision ~ where our models meet the outside record

Three models thrown at the field at once (Collision-Diver, 2026-09-08), then the sharpest finding collided against its own primary source. Each survivor tagged VINDICATE · CONTRADICT · EXTEND.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/strongest-ground>>

!! The strongest ground ~ the ontology arrived at twice, decades apart

''SPKI/SDSI (Rivest & Lampson 1996, RFC 2693) and KERI (Smith 2019) converged INDEPENDENTLY on our exact ontology.'' SDSI: names read LOCALLY, authority a KEY not a registry, a principal exports bindings ("Joe's poker-buddies") — identity-as-relation, standardized 27 years ago. KERI: self-certifying identifier · key-STATE as presenting authority · succession by GRAFTING the key-state (chained signed KEL) · identifier fixed for life · duplicity caught WITHOUT a clock. ''Two generations of security researchers reached the name-is-an-edge, the-authority-is-a-rolling-key-state, the-identifier-is-permanent-while-holders-are-not — from first principles.'' The model is where the field arrives when it takes decentralization seriously. Caution kept: SDSI LOST the market to X.509's global CAs — the better naming theory does not win on merit.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-coniks-resolution>>

!! The #1 exposure, RESOLVED at the source ~ equivocation-detection IS carriage

The collision named its own biggest threat: ''does carriage-not-registry forfeit equivocation-detection?'' — the CONIKS/Key-Transparency result that you catch a lying authority (one showing different keys to different readers) by publishing an append-only Merkle log. Collided against the primary paper (eprint 2014/1004):

''It DISSOLVES.'' CONIKS detects equivocation by ''GOSSIPING a COMPACT signed commitment (the Signed Tree Root), compared PER-READER'' — never by publishing the directory. //"users can detect if a provider is equivocating by comparing the STRs they receive."// A compact commitment, announced by the authority, replicated causally, compared as-of-each-reader's-view: ''that IS carriage.'' KERI reaches the same from the other side — two inconsistent KEL instances are provable duplicity, caught by WATCHERS who gossip what they saw. ''The registry filter survives whole.''

''What the collision actually surfaced — an OWED CAPABILITY, not a contradiction: WATCHERS.'' A per-reader view catches equivocation only if readers can COMPARE views — the gossip-of-what-you've-seen layer. We hold the duplicity-PROOF primitive (a veto out-competes as proof-of-contradiction, no clock); we have NOT built the watcher layer that circulates head-sightings so one reader catches a Handle showing quorum-A here and quorum-B there. ''The watcher gossips a signed "the head I saw for prefix X", which is carriage (a sighting announced by its observer), never a compiled who-is-who.''

''ITS HOME IS ALREADY DESIGNED (operator, 2026-09-08) — two layers that split exactly right:'' the ''Herm'' (the near-open crossroads relay, `carry⊥read`, sealed bytes — <<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/dreamnet-architecture>>) is the BLIND CARRIAGE: it forwards sighting-gossip like any bytes and cannot read it (the blind-relay integrity — a Herm diffuses, never watches). The ''Meshpalace'' (the Scope-1 CID/CAD/CRDT DreamNet gossip sensorium, the LAST palace, ITC/`getHeads`-shaped — the exact clock #golden-principles vindicated; `convergent-mesh` #three-clocks, `corpus` #organ) is the WATCHER'S HOME: a node's Meshpalace gossips a signed head-sighting, compares incoming sightings against its own view and the chain, and surfaces two-inconsistent-heads-for-one-prefix as a DUPLICITY PROOF the veto/fold already consumes (`identity-classes#the-two-forks`). So watchers = a Meshpalace-sensorium capability carried blind by Herms, registry-clean by construction. ⚠ ''CORRECTED at the substrate check (Meme-Warden, 2026-09-08):'' the watcher is NOT "a wire onto designed ground" — that overstated readiness. The mesh-palace FLOW-map STANDS (`mesh-palace.ts`, a routing chart: dial-records, cap-stacks, route slots) but it is the MAP, not the sensorium — it carries no head-sightings, no view-comparison, no duplicity surface. The Meshpalace SENSORIUM (the ITC/getHeads-shaped DreamNet gossip instance, the watcher's true home) ''does NOT stand in code'' — no `meshpalace_io`, no gossip router. The pieces that DO stand: the ITC primitive (`itc.ts`), `detectDuplicity` (`wax-stamp.ts`), and the veto/`foldPersonaContests` that CONSUME a duplicity once two inconsistent events already sit in a chain. What is missing is the layer that GOSSIPS head-sightings to surface that inconsistency across the mesh. ''Honest reading: watchers await a WHOLE PALACE — the federation-last sensorium — not a wire.'' The home is named and the primitives are proven; the palace is unbuilt.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/golden-principles>>

!! Golden principles the field converged on ~ hold these

* ''NO-GLOBAL-NOW is a hardware law, not a preference'' (FLP 1985 · CAP · PACELC 2010). Deterministic consensus is impossible under pure asynchrony with one crash fault; the only escapes are randomization, partial synchrony, or WEAKENED liveness. We chose weakened liveness (φ-accrual) and are honest about it. EXTEND — ''PACELC names the tax at peace:'' even with no partition you still trade Latency for Consistency. We stand PA/EL — ''a linearizable read is one we can NEVER offer.'' Say so at every gate.
* ''Fork/join membership without a roster is PROVEN in theory'' — Interval Tree Clocks (Almeida-Baquero-Fonte 2008), VERIFIED at the primary source (eprint fetch 2026-09-08): fork produces two clones with disjoint event ids that evolve independently, join merges them, event increments locally — "no global coordination or central authority required for generating unique identifiers." Our quorum-rollover has a sound clock-shape underneath it. ⚠ ''CORRECTION:'' the earlier "in production (Riak, Akka)" claim rode a search-summary and the ITC PAPER makes NO deployment claim — struck as unverified (and likely erroneous: Riak ships DOTTED VERSION VECTORS, not ITC). The vindication is the MECHANISM (proven, cited), never a deployment (unproven, withdrawn).
* ''Weak subjectivity names the boundary'' (Buterin 2014): a node offline past a horizon cannot self-heal from cryptography alone — it needs an out-of-band social checkpoint. Matches our "beyond horizon K a lone island asks a human." And the 2024 caution: DON'T overload social consensus.
* ''Data-protection-by-architecture'' (GDPR Art. 25): pseudonymization-by-default, minimize extent/period/accessibility. Our rejection-law reads as a COMPLIANCE posture, not only an aesthetic.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/anti-patterns>>

!! Anti-patterns ~ measured graves, do not dig them

* ''SSB's FROZEN IDENTITY (the builder-risk we already escaped).'' Secure Scuttlebutt bound identity to ONE keypair on an append-only log and shipped NO rotation: a compromised key appends to your log forever; the only cure is a NEW identity, losing every social tie. ''This is the grave of getting succession wrong under carriage.'' We escaped it BY CONSTRUCTION — the name binds a ROLLING QUORUM (the Mu), not a fixed key; the rolling recovery commitment + armed inception are the KERI-pre-rotation SSB lacked. Note it as the thing our design exists to avoid.
* ''SILENCE IS AMBIGUOUS'' (TUF freshness). A withheld update and a slow link look identical, so observer-local hardening-by-silence must BOUND the wait or an attacker freezes a victim indefinitely by withholding. SHARPENS the φ-accrual clause: silence-across-K-local-epochs needs the local epochs to genuinely ADVANCE and an explicit bound — the idle-mesh edge, now doubly flagged.
* ''SYBIL RINGS blend into the social graph'' (BrightID-measured). A k-of-n Handle is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a self-vouching sybil ring; graph defense has a measured hole for small sophisticated rings. The cost-dial (rb>c, the voucher co-pays) PRICES sybil, never eliminates it — already canon, re-confirmed.
* ''ACL/registry thinking drags back the CONFUSED DEPUTY'' (Miller). Any residual place that enumerates holders IS an ACL and re-imports ambient authority. Carriage-not-registry is the security-correct choice, not only the private one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/pattern-integrities>>

!! Pattern-integrities ~ the waves, not the water

* ''LOCAL NAMES over GLOBAL IDENTIFIERS'' — recurs identically in contact lists, SDSI, petnames, Nostr NIP-05, DNS-read-adversarially. Human-meaningful naming is ALWAYS a local overlay on a machine-meaningful identifier; fuse them and you get phishing (DNS) or unmemorable keys. Our Handle-over-edge is this wave.
* ''IMPROPER NAMES'' (Deseriis) — the k-of-n Handle is a STUDIED social form, not a novelty, and gives us vocabulary: a ''multiple-use name'' (Luther Blissett — hundreds sharing one open name, 1994–99, then VOLUNTARILY RETIRED — a deliberate succession) vs a ''collective pseudonym'' (Wu Ming — a specific controlled group). Maps EXACTLY onto our 1-of-1-that-many-present vs k-of-n-chartered split. The Dread Pirate Roberts is a multiple-use name; a chartered cabal is a collective pseudonym.
* ''DUPLICITY-DETECTION is the deep DUAL of registry'' — CONIKS and KERI converge: you catch a lying authority not by consulting a registry of truth but by detecting EQUIVOCATION (two signed statements that cannot both be true). Our veto out-competes causally BECAUSE it is proof-of-contradiction, needing no clock. This is the wave; the watcher layer (#the-coniks-resolution) is the water it needs.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/standing-tensions>>

!! Standing tensions ~ what the field leaves genuinely open (operator-aware)

* ''MODERATION at scale.'' Hidden human-cardinality removes "ban the PERSON, not the account" — the primitive real-name policies wanted (and the Nymwars proved those policies HARM the vulnerable, so hiding cardinality is protective, and the abuse problem was never solved, only DEFERRED). Our partial answer: a ban propagates by CAPABILITY (kapae/antigen, the vouch-lineage slash), never by de-anonymizing. Honestly open — a k-of-n name a ban cannot reach one human behind is a real cost accepted for the pre-SIN stance.
* ''BENEFICIAL-OWNERSHIP LAW — DOCTRINE FIRMED (2026-09-08)'' (US CTA 2024 · EU AMLD). Where a Handle touches money or contracts, the law DEMANDS the who-is-who record our law forbids compiling. ''The two do not collide — they SEPARATE at the island wall:'' the sovereign carriage NEVER holds a KYC record (the registry filter holds absolutely inside the sovereign plane), and the legal/KYC record lives ENTIRELY at the WEB2 BRIDGE (`bridge-and-reach-plane`, operator-locked bridge scope; foreign credentials ride as `#has` caps held apart from the sovereign plane). ''A Handle that must be KYC'd does not leak its holders into carriage — it CROSSES into a contract plane whose legal record sits outside the sovereign wall, by construction a web2-bridge artifact behind a causal-island boundary'' (the web3-only law: any web2 bridge sits behind an island boundary; no web2 ontology enters the Lares stack proper). The DreamNet's own name for its holders stays unknowable; the LAW's record is a separate object in a separate plane. Named as doctrine; the contract-plane KYC artifact stands unbuilt (a declared red).

<<~/ahu>>

